  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Guardrail Dataset + Git Scorer = Aspect",
      "items": [
        "Publish datasets independently: input, label and strategy. Evaluation pins dataset and scorer versions, aspect and label mapping.",
        "Runner sends input to a Guardrail instance. Git script consumes input, normalized label, strategy and Scan output; it returns expected, predicted, outcome and reason.",
        "Unsafe is the positive class: TP = correct detection, FP = false alarm, TN = correct clearance, FN = missed detection. Results are aggregated for each binding."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Runtime and source boundaries",
      "items": [
        "Evaluation API creates a Kubernetes Job. The Runner container contains orchestration, Guardrail Proxy and Runner-local Collector.",
        "Git Repo groups the scorer source. The script is fetched at a pinned SHA and executed as a subprocess in Runner, not on the Git server.",
        "Guardrail Proxy represents HTTP Scan forwarding logic currently implemented in guardrail_worker; it is not a separately deployed proxy server. External targets are NeMo Guardrail / F5 instances, including Mock.",
        "LangSmith exporter is not implemented. Current scoring feedback and traces are stored in Elasticsearch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Telemetry, storage and credentials",
      "items": [
        "Three ES index families store resources/runs, samples/scores and traces. UI queries through Evaluation API.",
        "When OTel is configured, Runner exports standard OTLP spans. Typed sample and score feedback uses the Collector HTTP API. Cost is currently mock.",
        "Guardrail credentials use a protected run-detail endpoint. Git SSH keys are mounted from Secrets. Script subprocesses do not inherit API, Guardrail or Collector credentials.",
        "Based on a local working-tree evidence snapshot from 2026-11-04, not a published remote release commit."
      ]
    }
  ],
